## Request flow and sequence

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Browser
    participant FastAPI as FastAPI app
    participant Controller as src.api.controller.chat
    participant Sanitizer as src.utils.input_sanitizer
    participant Store as src.utils.conversation_store
    participant Factory as src.api.service.client_factory
    participant Provider as OpenAI / Gemini

    Browser->>FastAPI: GET / or POST /api/conversations
    FastAPI->>Controller: route request
    Controller->>Sanitizer: sanitize_message / sanitize_verification_claim
    Sanitizer-->>Controller: normalized input or validation error

    alt New chat or new message
        Controller->>Store: load_store()
        Store-->>Controller: conversation map
        Controller->>Factory: create_client(provider)
        Factory->>Provider: respond(prompt, previous_interaction_id)
        Provider-->>Factory: interaction id + model reply
        Factory-->>Controller: ClientResponse
        Controller->>Store: save_store(updated history)
        Store-->>Controller: confirm write
        Controller-->>Browser: JSON response with answer and metadata
    else Verify claim against history
        Controller->>Store: load_store()
        Store-->>Controller: conversation record
        Controller->>Factory: create_client(provider)
        Factory->>Provider: verify prompt with prior interaction id
        Provider-->>Factory: interaction id + evidence-based answer
        Factory-->>Controller: ClientResponse
        Controller->>Store: save_store(updated history)
        Controller-->>Browser: verification response
    end
```

## Setup

Create a virtual environment, install the project in editable mode, and install runtime dependencies:

```powershell
python -m venv .venv
.\.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
pip install -e .
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

Set provider keys in the project root `.env` file. Add only the provider keys you plan to use:

```env
GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key
OPENAI_API_KEY=your_openai_api_key
```

The `.env` file is ignored by Git. Do not commit API keys.

## Run

From the project root:

```powershell
python main.py --reload
```

Open <http://127.0.0.1:8000> in a browser. Select a provider for a new chat. The UI includes
separate views for the current conversation, saved history, and checking a claim against the
selected conversation. Use New chat to create a new conversation thread.

Messages and verification claims are normalized and validated before they reach a provider.
The app rejects blocked profanity terms and common instruction-override patterns. Set
`CHAT_BLOCKED_TERMS` to a comma-separated list to override the default profanity terms. This is a
lightweight input filter, not a full content-moderation or prompt-injection prevention system.

Saved conversations are written to the ignored `data/gemini_conversations.json` file. Rotating
application logs are written under the ignored `logs/` directory. The runtime-data folder is kept
separate from source files so generated state does not crowd the project root. The legacy
`uvicorn app:app --reload` command remains supported for compatibility with older workflows.
Older standalone demos are kept under `tests/manual/`.
